{%- comment -%}
  Mirrors ../design-system/src/react/Text/Text.tsx: a single text node whose typography role and
  colour variant come straight from the design system's --text-role-* / --text-color-* tokens.

  A different file, blocks/text.liquid, is Horizon's built-in "Text" block (t:names.text) -- an
  editorial rich-text block with its own custom-size typography system flowing through
  snippets/design-system-bridge.liquid. This block does not touch that one -- it exposes the
  design system's fixed role/variant vocabulary directly, rather than bridging it onto Horizon's
  own presets. This block is named "Mionas: Text" in the block picker to
  distinguish it from "Text" (Variant/Size/Color/HTML tag settings here, vs. Type preset there).
  See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-20-text-role-block-design.md (written when this block was
  still named "Mionas: Text role").

  Variant and Size are separate settings, 1:1 with Text.tsx's own `variant` (band: display,
  headline, title, body, label) and `size` (lg/md/sm) props -- they used to be one combined
  `role` select (e.g. "display-lg"). snippets/mionas-text.liquid takes the same two params
  separately and joins them internally; this block just passes them straight through. Color keeps
  its own axis, same as Text.tsx's `color` prop -- it was also called `variant` here before this
  split, which would have collided with the new band setting, so it was renamed to `color` to
  match the design system's own prop name.

  The CSS class prefix (`text-role`) and the --text-role-*/--text-color-* tokens keep their names --
  they mirror the design system's own Text.tsx `role` vocabulary, not this block's editor label.

  `tag` is independent of Variant/Size, same as Text.tsx's `as` prop is independent of `variant`/
  `size` -- a label-styled span or an h2 with hero styling are both valid.

  The Text setting is `richtext` so copy can span several lines, but its block-level markup is
  flattened to `<br>` before output by snippets/mionas-inline-richtext.liquid, which documents why.
  blocks/mionas-stamp.liquid flattens through the same snippet.

  Trade-off of that flattening: the theme editor only live-previews a text setting when it's output
  unfiltered and alone inside its element, so typing here re-renders the section instead of updating
  instantly. Keeping bold/italic/link on existing copy is worth that -- the alternative (a plain
  `textarea` output unfiltered, with `white-space: pre-line`) would drop inline formatting.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign block_settings = block.settings
  assign tag = block_settings.tag | default: 'p'
%}
{%- capture content %}{% render 'mionas-inline-richtext', value: block_settings.text %}{% endcapture -%}
{% liquid
  assign content = content | strip

  # An "empty" richtext value is `<p></p>` or `<p><br></p>` -- not blank -- so gate on the visible
  # text, the same way snippets/text.liquid does, or the block emits an empty element.
  assign visible_text = content | strip_html | strip
%}

{%- comment -%}
  The element itself, and the text-role classes on it, come from snippets/mionas-text.liquid. This
  block is now the settings-and-richtext half of the pair: it owns the visible-text gate, the schema,
  and the .text-role CSS below, which stays here rather than moving to the snippet because snippets
  cannot declare a stylesheet tag.

  blocks/mionas-price.liquid renders the same snippet with its own dynamic content, so the role
  vocabulary has one implementation rather than one per block.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if visible_text != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    `spacing-style` is Horizon's own class (base.css:1352-1381): it turns the four --padding-* custom
    properties the snippet writes into real padding, with 0px fallbacks, and scales anything above
    20px responsively. Same mechanism, same four setting ids, as blocks/mionas-price.liquid and
    blocks/mionas-add-to-cart.liquid, so a merchant insets a text block the way they inset every
    other block in the theme rather than reaching for a group wrapper.

    No .text-role rule declares padding, so `spacing-style`'s (0,1,0) padding in base.css has nothing
    in this bundle to lose source order to -- nothing here needs to be two classes deep.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture text_style -%}
    {%- render 'spacing-style', settings: block_settings -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- render 'mionas-text',
    content: content,
    variant: block_settings.variant,
    size: block_settings.size,
    color: block_settings.color,
    tag: tag,
    class: 'spacing-style',
    style: text_style,
    shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes
  -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .text-role {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-family-archivo);
  }

  /* One class per text-role token, 1:1 with Text.tsx's band x size grid: five bands at three
     sizes each. All fifteen are exposed even though the theme only uses nine, because this block
     is the theme's mirror of Text -- a mirror offering a subset would quietly be a different
     component. Keep the `variant`/`size` selects' options and snippets/mionas-text.liquid's
     whitelist in step with this list.

     These names replaced a flat ten-role vocabulary; the old-to-new table is in
     docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-20-text-role-block-design.md, which is also what stored
     settings were migrated by. */
  .text-role--display-lg {
    font-size: var(--text-role-display-lg-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-display-lg-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-display-lg-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-display-lg-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--display-md {
    font-size: var(--text-role-display-md-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-display-md-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-display-md-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-display-md-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--display-sm {
    font-size: var(--text-role-display-sm-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-display-sm-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-display-sm-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-display-sm-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--headline-lg {
    font-size: var(--text-role-headline-lg-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-headline-lg-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-headline-lg-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-headline-lg-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--headline-md {
    font-size: var(--text-role-headline-md-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-headline-md-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-headline-md-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-headline-md-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--headline-sm {
    font-size: var(--text-role-headline-sm-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-headline-sm-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-headline-sm-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-headline-sm-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--title-lg {
    font-size: var(--text-role-title-lg-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-title-lg-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-title-lg-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-title-lg-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--title-md {
    font-size: var(--text-role-title-md-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-title-md-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-title-md-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-title-md-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--title-sm {
    font-size: var(--text-role-title-sm-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-title-sm-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-title-sm-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-title-sm-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--body-lg {
    font-size: var(--text-role-body-lg-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-body-lg-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-body-lg-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-body-lg-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--body-md {
    font-size: var(--text-role-body-md-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-body-md-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-body-md-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-body-md-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--body-sm {
    font-size: var(--text-role-body-sm-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-body-sm-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-body-sm-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-body-sm-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--label-lg {
    font-size: var(--text-role-label-lg-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-label-lg-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-label-lg-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-label-lg-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--label-md {
    font-size: var(--text-role-label-md-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-label-md-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-label-md-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-label-md-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--label-sm {
    font-size: var(--text-role-label-sm-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-label-sm-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-label-sm-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-label-sm-letter-spacing);
  }

  /* There is deliberately no sixteenth rule here for Stamp. It is a component in ../design-system
     (src/react/Stamp/Stamp.tsx), not a text role -- a role bundle cannot carry a typeface, a
     transform or its wide tracking -- so it is blocks/mionas-stamp.liquid, which COMPOSES the label
     roles above (its Size setting picks one) rather than adding a role beside them, exactly as
     Stamp.tsx renders `<Text variant="label" size={size}>`. Nothing in the theme spends a
     .text-role--stamp class any more; the four --stamp-base-* tokens are spent by that block. */

  .text-role--default {
    color: var(--text-color-default);
  }

  .text-role--primary {
    color: var(--text-color-primary);
  }

  .text-role--inverse-primary {
    color: var(--text-color-inverse-primary);
  }

  .text-role--inverse-primary-muted {
    color: var(--text-color-inverse-primary-muted);
  }

  .text-role--accent {
    color: var(--text-color-accent);
  }

  .text-role--accent-inverse {
    color: var(--text-color-accent-inverse);
  }

  .text-role--tint {
    color: var(--text-color-tint);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Text role",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "<p>Text</p>",
      "info": "Press Enter for a line break; it renders inside the same element, not as a new paragraph."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "variant",
      "label": "Variant",
      "options": [
        { "value": "display", "label": "Display" },
        { "value": "headline", "label": "Headline" },
        { "value": "title", "label": "Title" },
        { "value": "body", "label": "Body" },
        { "value": "label", "label": "Label" }
      ],
      "default": "body",
      "info": "The typography band, same as Text.tsx's `variant` prop."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "size",
      "label": "Size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "lg", "label": "Large" },
        { "value": "md", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "sm", "label": "Small" }
      ],
      "default": "md",
      "info": "The step within the Variant band."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "color",
      "label": "Color",
      "options": [
        { "value": "default", "label": "Default" },
        { "value": "primary", "label": "Primary" },
        { "value": "inverse-primary", "label": "Inverse primary" },
        { "value": "inverse-primary-muted", "label": "Inverse primary (muted)" },
        { "value": "accent", "label": "Accent" },
        { "value": "accent-inverse", "label": "Accent (inverse)" },
        { "value": "tint", "label": "Tint" }
      ],
      "default": "default"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "tag",
      "label": "HTML tag",
      "options": [
        { "value": "p", "label": "p" },
        { "value": "span", "label": "span" },
        { "value": "div", "label": "div" },
        { "value": "h1", "label": "h1" },
        { "value": "h2", "label": "h2" },
        { "value": "h3", "label": "h3" },
        { "value": "h4", "label": "h4" },
        { "value": "h5", "label": "h5" },
        { "value": "h6", "label": "h6" }
      ],
      "default": "p",
      "info": "Pick the semantic level; it doesn't have to match Variant."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-start",
      "label": "t:settings.left",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-end",
      "label": "t:settings.right",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Text",
      "category": "t:categories.basic"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
